{{!--
    What requires what, as columns — and, underneath, what requires nothing.

    A Thread sits one column right of its deepest prerequisite, so every arrow
    points rightward and none of them doubles back — the layering is decided in
    logic/graph-layout.mjs and this template only draws what it was handed.

    THE ARROWS ARE NOT HERE. Only the browser knows where a card landed once the
    text has wrapped and the panel has been resized, so the curves are drawn into
    the <svg> below in _onRender, measured off the cards. Each card carries the
    ids it requires in `data-requires`, which is why there is no serialised edge
    list in this markup: an id sitting on the card that owns it cannot be
    mispaired, and a JSON blob in an attribute is one escaping bug from a blank
    board.

    THE LOOSE THREADS ARE CARDS NOW, NOT A COUNT. They used to be a sentence
    saying how many had been left out, on the reasoning that cards with no arrow
    on them bury the ones that have them. That reasoning holds for the COLUMNS
    and nowhere else — so they are drawn below the diagram instead of inside it,
    where they cannot push a chain off the side of the screen and where "these
    are waiting on nobody" is a useful answer rather than a missing one.
--}}

{{!-- One box for both readings of this Plot: the query is shared with the
      Threads list, so a name typed here is still typed there. In the list it
      hides the rows that do not match; here it hides every chain that does not
      contain a match, because half a chain is a lie about what is blocking
      what. --}}
{{#if openPlot.hasManyThreads}}
{{> "modules/remito-situation-room/templates/partials/search-bar.hbs" scope="graph"
    placeholder="RSR.search.threadsPlaceholder"}}
{{/if}}

<div class="rsr-graph" data-search-list="graph">

    {{#if openPlot.graph.hasEdges}}
    <div class="rsr-graph-canvas">
        <svg class="rsr-graph-edges" aria-hidden="true"></svg>

        <div class="rsr-graph-layers">
            {{#each openPlot.graph.layers}}
            <div class="rsr-graph-layer">
                {{#each this.cards}}
                {{> "modules/remito-situation-room/templates/partials/graph-card.hbs"}}
                {{/each}}
            </div>
            {{/each}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{else}}
    {{!-- No arrows anywhere. The loose Threads below are the whole of this
          Plot, and saying so is kinder than drawing them under a heading that
          implies something was left out. --}}
    <p class="rsr-empty rsr-graph-nothing">{{localize "RSR.graph.none"}}</p>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- Threads in a ring, or waiting behind one. They can never open, so they
          are named outright rather than drawn in a column that would imply an
          order they do not have. --}}
    {{#if openPlot.graph.tangled.length}}
    <p class="rsr-graph-tangle">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" inert></i>
        {{localize "RSR.graph.tangled"}}
        {{#each openPlot.graph.tangled}}<em>{{this}}</em>{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
    </p>
    {{/if}}

    {{#if openPlot.graph.loose.length}}
    <section class="rsr-graph-free">
        <h4 class="rsr-graph-free-title">
            {{localize "RSR.graph.looseTitle"}}
            <span class="rsr-count">{{openPlot.graph.loose.length}}</span>
        </h4>
        <div class="rsr-graph-free-cards">
            {{#each openPlot.graph.loose}}
            {{> "modules/remito-situation-room/templates/partials/graph-card.hbs"}}
            {{/each}}
        </div>
    </section>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- Every card is still in the view, hidden. Without this a search that
          matches nothing reads as a Plot whose requirements have vanished. --}}
    <p class="rsr-empty rsr-search-empty" data-search-empty="graph" hidden>
        {{localize "RSR.search.none"}}
    </p>
</div>
